Working entry: «Granular API-error cause» — an API-error turn end names its cause from a closed list of nine words;
the error text still crosses nothing (v2-34). Epoch 3 — Driver reliability: turns and sends, its last entry before
«Scheduled-wake count on a turn end».

- The masters hold the rows naming the one word and the adapter-only classes: architecture
  `contract/turn-end-cause/cause-set`, `contract/event-data/turn-ended-cause`, `contract/hook-to-kind-map/stopfailure`;
  security-plan `decision/api-error-classes-adapter-only`, `decision/api-error-turn-end-text-dropped`,
  `contract/channel-frames/hook-event-revalidation`; design-system `decision/api-error-turn-end-shown-as-turn-end`;
  test-plan `contract/event-data/turn-ended` (its key, no value list). They are the wrap's reconcile.

- **Thresholds.** The chunk adds no numeric threshold. The booted case's waits are WITHIN = 12 s, below the mutants
  profile's 15 s kill and cargo-mutants' 20 s floor `(test-plan · bootstrap-phases-derive-for-route-setup-project/decision/mutants-kill-below-cargo-mutants-timeout)`;
  each control's `--timeout` sits above its filtered entry's own run time and below nothing a mutant reaches.
